I see boulder traps with the boulder a space or two
outside a doorway on an extremely regular basis, I'm
a bit bemused that others are finding this to be a
"rare" event.

Having both travel ends possibly outside the room,
as in the revised diagram Raisse gave (but
presumably the game "froze" at the point where her
PC died, and so never confirmed that the other end
of the boulder's traverse was outside on the left)
is probably rare just from the odds against a trap
and a room with doors aligned on opposite walls in
any case happening together, but I seem to recall
having seen at least one of those, too.

What I'd like to see treated as a bug, though, is
generating a boulder trap whose path crosses the
bottom of a stairway. That's too highly likely to
be a YAAD for my taste.

As for "avoiding the YAAD", yes, it was surely
possible, by searching the room thoroughly for traps
before inviting the pet downstairs, but since
NetHack's searching is so low-return, high effort
(someone just posted, IIRC, that it takes 30
searches to be 99% sure of having detected a trap in
the surrounding 8 grid cells), that would in turn
risk starving or having the pet go feral, so
probably just taking the risk of such a deadfall and
dying once in a while is the odds-on high survival
rate approach on a "many games" basis.

